  "verbalization": "Borapetoside D is implicated in the biological pathway leading to SNB-78 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Borapetoside D directly targets hepatocytes, which are then targeted by other compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, which in turn targets SNB-78. This indicates a chain of molecular interactions where Borapetoside D acts as a starting point, with subsequent targets in the pathway contributing to the final effect on SNB-78. The presence of multiple intermediate targets, including a complex and lengthy compound, suggests that the relationship between Borapetoside D and SNB-78 is mediated through a series of steps involving hepatocytes and other molecules. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network, where the direct interaction between Borapetoside D and SNB-78 may be indirectly supported by the presence of these intermediaries.",
